<problem>
<!-- <title>Discrete equilibria with parameters, factored cubic polynomial</title> -->

<setup>

<select name="difference_form" type="boolean">true false</select>

<select name="n"> n t</select>
<select name="a" numToSelect="6" withReplacement="false"> s u v w a b c d k m p q r</select>

<select name="x">
<option selectWeight="1">x</option>
<option selectWeight="1">y</option>
<option selectWeight="1">z</option>
<option selectWeight="13">$a[6]</option>
</select>

<math name="equilibria" unordered="true">$a[2] ,$a[3] ,$a[4] </math>

</setup>


<p>For the dynamical system

<md>
  <mrow>$x _{ $n +1}
    <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$difference_form">-$x _$n  </case>
    </conditionalContent>
  \amp = $a[1] ($x _$n -$a[2] )($x _$n -$a[3] )($x _$n -$a[4] )
    <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="not $difference_form">+ $x _$n  </case>
    </conditionalContent>
  </mrow>
  <mrow>$x _0\amp = $a[5] ,</mrow>
</md>
for parameters <m>$a[1] </m>, <m>$a[2] </m>, <m>$a[3] </m>, <m>$a[4] </m>, and <m>$a[5] </m>, with <m>$a[1]  \ne 0</m>, what are the equilibria?

</p>

<p>Equilibria: 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" symbolicEquality="true">$equilibria </award>
</answer>

If there is more than one equilibrium, separate answers by commas.
</p>


<solution>


To find the equilibria, set <m>$x _{ $n +1}=$x _$n  = E</m>.
<md>
  <mrow>E
    <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$difference_form">-E</case>
    </conditionalContent>
  \amp = $a[1] (E-$a[2] )(E-$a[3] )(E-$a[4] )
    <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="not $difference_form">+E</case>
    </conditionalContent>
  </mrow>
  <mrow>0\amp = $a[1] (E-$a[2] )(E-$a[3] )(E-$a[4] )</mrow>
</md>

Since <m>$a[1]  \ne 0</m>, this polynomial in <m>E</m> can be zero only if <m>E-$a[2] =0</m>, <m>E-$a[3] =0</m>, or <m>E-$a[4] =0</m>.  The three equilibria are <m>E=$a[2] </m>, <m>E=$a[3] </m>, and <m>E=$a[4] </m>.

</solution>


</problem>